<title>USA: Mallinckrodt says Hoechst unit drops suit.</title>
<headline>Mallinckrodt says Hoechst unit drops suit.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mallinckrodt Inc said New Jersey-based Hoechst Roussel Vet agreed to drop a lawsuit against Mallinckrodt and investment banker J.P. Morgan filed shortly after Mallinckrodt announced it intended to sell its veterinary division.</p>
<p>Hoechst Roussel, a unit of Hoechst AG, said it filed the suit to protect exclusive rights it has relating to certain vaccines and biological reagents. These rights are specified under agreements Hoechst entered into with Syntro Corp and Syntro Vet Inc, which are now owned by Mallinckrodt.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
